# You design and build LEGO Technic models one step at a time, in a build language.
#
# For each step you write:
# ADD name partnumber color
# CONNECT part.point -> part.point LOCKED|TURNS|STIFF   (points: hole1.., axlehole1.., pin1.., axle1.., clip1..; LOCKED = cross in cross, turn together; TURNS = free; STIFF = friction pin)
# Optional: MESH a.teeth b.teeth / RATIO a b x/y / GROUP g (opens a side build) / END (closes it) / ATTACH g (joins a finished side build into the main model)
# WHY one plain sentence: what this step builds and what it is for.
# A point ending in ~ is an estimate; ? means not known.
#
# Rules: only use real points of each part; a round pin never goes in a cross hole; a shaft that must turn needs round holes; a worm needs stops on both sides; gears must sit at the right distance.
STEP 1
ADD hub-core1 92907 black
ADD hub-ax1 32073 lightgray
ADD hub-ax2 4519 lightgray
CONNECT hub-ax1.axle1~ -> hub-core1.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT hub-ax2.axle1~ -> hub-core1.axlehole2~ LOCKED
WHY Locks a long axle into the split cross-connector and a second long axle, starting the hub at the centre of the snowmobile.
STEP 2
ADD hub-ax3 3706 black
ADD hub-ax4 87083 darkgray
CONNECT hub-ax3.axle1~ -> hub-core1.axlehole3~ LOCKED
CONNECT hub-ax4.axle1~ -> hub-core1.axlehole4~ LOCKED
WHY Locks the third and fourth axles into the remaining two arms of the split connector, completing the four-way cross.
STEP 3
ADD hub-end1 92907 black
ADD hub-end2 92907 black
ADD hub-end3 92907 black
CONNECT hub-end1.axlehole1~ -> hub-ax1.axle4~ LOCKED
CONNECT hub-end2.axlehole1~ -> hub-ax2.axle2~ LOCKED
CONNECT hub-end3.axlehole1~ -> hub-ax3.axle4~ LOCKED
WHY Caps three of the four hub arms with a second split connector each, giving every arm a socket for the body beams that follow.
STEP 4
ADD hub-end4 32184 black
ADD hub-brace1 60483 darkgray
ADD hub-brace2 60483 darkgray
ADD hub-stub1 32062 red
ADD hub-stub2 32062 red
CONNECT hub-end4.axlehole1~ -> hub-ax4.axle3~ LOCKED
CONNECT hub-stub1.axle1~ -> hub-brace1.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT hub-stub1.axle2~ -> hub-core1.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT hub-stub2.axle1~ -> hub-brace2.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT hub-stub2.axle2~ -> hub-core1.axlehole2~ LOCKED
WHY Caps the fourth hub arm with a perpendicular connector and adds two small bracket beams, ready to carry the ski arms and track bogies.
STEP 5
ADD skiL-bent1 32271 black
ADD skiL-pin1 2780 black
CONNECT skiL-pin1.pin1~ -> hub-end1.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT skiL-pin1.pin2~ -> skiL-bent1.hole1~ STIFF
WHY Starts the left ski arm: a bent beam pinned to the perpendicular connector capping the hub's forward arm.
